---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Results & Retired Claims"
  description="Agalmic Research results, negative findings, narrowed claims and retired novelty claims, separated from research infrastructure and exploratory possibilities."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Results · corrections · retirements</p>
      <h1>What has the inquiry actually changed?</h1>
      <p class="lede">Methods, provenance, taxonomies and research interfaces are infrastructure. This page records the smaller set of outcomes where prior art, formalization, evidence, criticism or implementation has constrained a claim.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell thesis">
      <p class="eyebrow">Result rule</p>
      <blockquote>A result is something the programme is less free to believe after the inquiry than before it.</blockquote>
      <p>Positive findings count. So do failed novelty claims, null results, narrowed definitions, abandoned mechanisms and evidence that a simpler existing explanation is sufficient.</p>
      <p>Items here may still be internal working results rather than peer-reviewed scientific findings. Their epistemic status is stated explicitly.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="section-number">Current record</span>
        <div class="section-copy">
          <h2>Claims that have already become narrower.</h2>
          <p>The point is not to accumulate defeats. It is to make it visible when the machinery actually bites.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="index-list">
        <article class="index-item">
          <span class="index-meta">R01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Generic epistemic handoff is not a novel institution.</h3>
            <p>Absorptive capacity, knowledge transfer, knowledge brokerage, innovation intermediaries, transactive memory and idea-evaluation research already cover the generic problem of moving knowledge toward actors able to use or evaluate it.</p>
            <p><strong>What survived:</strong> a narrower claim-sensitive protocol that makes the authority deficit, requested epistemic function, contribution provenance and resulting warrant explicit.</p>
            <p><a href="/drafts/epistemic-handoff/">Inspect the narrowed draft →</a></p>
          </div>
          <span class="index-status">narrowed</span>
        </article>

        <article class="index-item">
          <span class="index-meta">R02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Expert-attention triage is established; the allocation test remains open.</h3>
            <p>AI-assisted idea screening, selective prediction, learning to defer, active learning, editorial triage and value-of-information already establish the generic mechanism of protecting expensive human evaluation with cheaper screening.</p>
            <p><strong>What remains:</strong> test whether a provenance- and authority-aware routing policy can increase useful epistemic state change per expert-hour while controlling false negatives, status bias and presentation gaming.</p>
            <p><a href="/drafts/handoff-triage-formalism/">Inspect the formalism and test →</a></p>
          </div>
          <span class="index-status">open test</span>
        </article>

        <article class="index-item">
          <span class="index-meta">R03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>The economics of epistemic abundance has not yet produced a distinct economic primitive.</h3>
            <p>The current formal-null review finds mature antecedents in production economics, complementarity, bottlenecks, innovation theory, production networks and rebound effects. The programme therefore does not presently claim a new law or primitive merely because AI makes candidate knowledge cheaper.</p>
            <p><strong>What survived:</strong> an empirical question about how binding constraints, shadow values and rents move when a previously costly capability becomes cheap.</p>
            <p><a href="/frontier/">See its current option status →</a></p>
          </div>
          <span class="index-status">null / option</span>
        </article>

        <article class="index-item">
          <span class="index-meta">R04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>The effective adjacent possible is inherited vocabulary, not Agalmic terminology.</h3>
            <p>The programme's innovation-search work now treats the adjacent possible and effective adjacent possible as established antecedents rather than territorial novelty claims.</p>
            <p><strong>What survived:</strong> the practical question of how machine cognition changes search breadth, recognition, validation, assimilation and realization.</p>
            <p><a href="/lineage/">Inspect the lineage register →</a></p>
          </div>
          <span class="index-status">novelty retired</span>
        </article>

        <article class="index-item">
          <span class="index-meta">R05</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Nemosyne cannot validate the whole Agalmic programme.</h3>
            <p>Software can test bounded claims about representation, analyst performance, provenance interfaces, cognitive burden and discovery workflows. It cannot by itself establish macroeconomic claims about displaced scarcity, institutional allocation or economy-wide abundance.</p>
            <p><strong>What survived:</strong> Nemosyne as an experimental instrument for the claims its interventions can actually identify.</p>
            <p><a href="/manifesto/">See the applied-research boundary →</a></p>
          </div>
          <span class="index-status">boundary set</span>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What does not belong here</p>
        <h2>Scaffolding is not a finding.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>A provenance schema, Memory Palace representation, handoff register, Active Frontier, possibility portfolio or website architecture can be useful infrastructure. Its existence is not evidence that the underlying research claims are true.</p>
        <p>Those systems earn their keep by making inquiry cheaper, clearer or more falsifiable. If they consume more attention than they save, they should be simplified or removed.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Retirement discipline</p>
        <h2>Lineage is allowed to kill our words.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>When a proposed Agalmic concept collapses cleanly into established theory, the default response is to use the established theory. The question may remain interesting even when the local label does not.</p>
        <div class="callout"><p><strong>A failed novelty claim is evidence that prior-art search worked.</strong></p></div>
        <p>Future retired claims and negative results should be added here rather than quietly disappearing from the public record.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
